sub:Head {
  this: a np:Nanopublication ;
    np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
    np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
    np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/scaling-bending-law> a delphi:Concept, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Bending strength of an isometric member via the section modulus (R9) (Lean 4, kernel-checked)" ;
    dct:description "For a slender linear-elastic beam with similar sections and lever arm proportional to size, bending stress scales as L when the load scales as the body (and a size limit σ_max k_Z/(k_F k_ℓ n) follows) and is independent of size when the load scales as an area (no limit follows)." ;
    dct:source "Proved in this project (lean/Delphi/Scaling.lean) from the physics thread's formal statements (physics/FORMAL-STATEMENTS.md, 2026-10-31; Galileo 1638 and Thompson 1917 ch. II for the idea); hypotheses named, no paper states it in this form." ;
    skos:notation "σ_b = F ℓ / Z ; R9a: σ_b ∝ L, L_max,b = σ_max k_Z/(k_F k_ℓ n) ; R9b: σ_b ∝ L^0" ;
    skos:definition """/-- **R9a, conclusion 1 (body-like load).** With the load scaling as the body (`CubeLaw F`), lever arm `∝ L` and similar sections (`Z ∝ L³`), bending stress scales as `L`. -/
theorem bendingStress_ratio_body {F ℓ Z : ℝ → ℝ} {kF kℓ kZ : ℝ} (hF : CubeLaw F kF) (hℓ : LeverLaw ℓ kℓ)
    (hZ : SectionModulusLaw Z kZ) {L₁ L₂ : ℝ} (h₁ : 0 < L₁) (h₂ : 0 < L₂) :
    bendingStress F ℓ Z L₂ / bendingStress F ℓ Z L₁ = L₂ / L₁"""^^delphi:lean4 ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    delphi:leanDeclaration "Delphi.bendingStress" ;
    delphi:leanTheorem "Delphi.bendingStress_ratio_body", "Delphi.bendingStress_log_body", "Delphi.bendingSafety_eq", "Delphi.bending_cannot_carry", "Delphi.bendingStress_ratio_sheet", "Delphi.bendingStress_log_sheet" ;
    delphi:leanVerified "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    skos:scopeNote "Slender linear-elastic beam theory, geometrically similar sections, lever arm ∝ L and constant σ_max are named hypotheses; elastic similarity (d ∝ ℓ^(3/2)) and dynamic loads such as wind are not formalised." ;
    rdfs:comment "Status: kernel-checked (Lean 4 accepted the module with zero sorry and standard axioms only). Not expert-validated. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it; strict neutrality, constant population size, Wright-Fisher reproduction and independent mutant fates (Kimura), fixed fitnesses and haploid inheritance (Fisher), equal fecundity and a 1:1 sex ratio (Maynard Smith) are assumptions written in the module header, not conclusions. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the paper is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/Delphi/Scaling.lean>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/scaling-bending-law> dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/scaling-bending-law> ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-scaling-bending-law> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-scaling-bending-law> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Lean 4 kernel accepted Delphi.bendingStress_ratio_body with zero sorry and standard axioms, and rejected 3 deliberately broken variant(s)" ;
    dct:description "Build receipt. Lean (version 4.35.0, x86_64-w64-windows-gnu, commit eb6cafb7290e8bd5f2937522d8d804f58f02bafc, Release); toolchain leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0; Mathlib v4.35.0 (56a005855ea17e0b0958f73ec801ae140b0a1679). lake build exit 0 in 5.2 s with 0 errors; 0 sorry in lean/Delphi/Scaling.lean (320 lines). #print axioms for Delphi.bendingStress_ratio_body, Delphi.bendingStress_log_body, Delphi.bendingSafety_eq, Delphi.bending_cannot_carry, Delphi.bendingStress_ratio_sheet, Delphi.bendingStress_log_sheet: Classical.choice, Quot.sound, propext only (Lean's standard axioms; no sorryAx). Mutation evidence (lean/mutate.mjs, 2026-10-31T19:28:19.294Z): 3 deliberate change(s) to the statement or the model were each rejected by the compiler: [bending-section-modulus-squared] R9 model mutant: the section modulus made to scale as d^2 instead of d^3 (then bending stress would scale as L^2 under a body-like load), so conclusion 1 must fail. Rejected with 4 error(s): bending-section-modulus-squared.lean:256:65: error: unsolved goals [bending-sheet-load-claims-body-conclusion] R9 mutant: the load made sheet-like (AreaLaw F) while conclusion 1 (stress proportional to L) is kept; it must fail, since a sheet-like load gives size-independent stress. Rejected with 3 error(s): bending-sheet-load-claims-body-conclusion.lean:256:65: error: unsolved goals [bending-limit-without-sigma] R9 mutant: the size limit stated without the material strength (threshold k_Z/(k_F k_l n)), conclusion 2 kept while sigma_max is dropped from the bound; it must fail. Rejected with 1 error(s): bending-limit-without-sigma.lean:288:2: error: linarith failed to find a contradiction Controls: 11 of 11 unmodified modules accepted by the same command." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/scaling-bending-law> ;
    rdfs:comment "This evidence item establishes that the stated theorem follows from the stated model. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it; strict neutrality, constant population size, Wright-Fisher reproduction and independent mutant fates (Kimura), fixed fitnesses and haploid inheritance (Fisher), equal fecundity and a 1:1 sex ratio (Maynard Smith) are assumptions written in the module header, not conclusions. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the paper is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/mutations.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/Delphi/Audit.lean> .
}

